WEBVTT

00:00:45.546 --> 00:00:48.799
<i>An unknown frontier</i>

00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:52.386
<i>On the map painted by my heart</i>

00:00:52.386 --> 00:00:59.142
<i>When I open the door, the path goes on</i>

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:05.107
<i>I'm kicking up dust as I</i>
<i>start running to your town</i>

00:01:05.107 --> 00:01:11.822
<i>Along a route where earth and sky meet</i>

00:01:11.822 --> 00:01:15.576
<i>Riding the rushing southern wind</i>

00:01:15.576 --> 00:01:18.495
<i>Slicing through the wind</i>
<i>dyed blue by the sky</i>

00:01:18.495 --> 00:01:25.627
<i>I'm rushing out with my whole heart</i>

00:01:25.627 --> 00:01:29.131
<i>Shooting past the midday moon</i>

00:01:29.131 --> 00:01:32.259
<i>Towards a world different</i>
<i>from what we've known before</i>

00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:36.096
<i>I will keep on running through to the end</i>

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.681
<i>However far</i>

00:01:37.681 --> 00:01:41.602
<i>Just like that wind</i>

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:46.899
<i>Just like that wind</i>

00:02:00.204 --> 00:02:04.249
"Left Behind"

00:02:08.212 --> 00:02:11.882
Wraith's taking over...
the entire mission?

00:02:15.219 --> 00:02:16.595
Where are you?

00:02:18.764 --> 00:02:21.558
Get out here, Wraith!
Talk to me!

00:02:21.558 --> 00:02:22.851
I know you're close by!

00:02:22.851 --> 00:02:24.895
How about answering me?

00:02:28.232 --> 00:02:30.150
I am Sergeant Sousuke Sagara.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:31.443
I am assigned to Mithril's
Tactical Division,

00:02:31.443 --> 00:02:34.154
the West Pacific Fleet "Tuatha de Danaan."

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:36.156
Under orders to guard a certain person,

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:38.909
I was dispatched to Tokyo as of April 20.

00:02:38.909 --> 00:02:42.371
It is possible this person is being
targeted for the following reasons.

00:02:42.371 --> 00:02:46.583
First! This individual is a special
kind of person called a "Whispered."

00:02:46.583 --> 00:02:49.336
Second! "Whispered" have
previously unknown knowledge,

00:02:49.336 --> 00:02:50.879
particularly relating to the military.

00:02:53.632 --> 00:02:55.300
Are you insane?

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.219
What kind of agent blurts
out top-secret information

00:02:57.219 --> 00:02:58.762
to the entire neighborhood
at the top of his voice?

00:02:58.762 --> 00:03:01.974
You are clearly sabotaging the operation!

00:03:01.974 --> 00:03:03.934
I only did it because<i> you </i>ignored me.

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:08.397
It's impossible for you not to understand how
dangerous it is for us to be talking like this.

00:03:08.397 --> 00:03:10.524
Uruz 7, what you are doing is...

00:03:10.524 --> 00:03:11.692
Answer me.

00:03:11.692 --> 00:03:15.779
Is your mission to guard Kaname
Chidori, or to observe her?

00:03:15.779 --> 00:03:17.489
I have no obligation to answer that.

00:03:17.489 --> 00:03:21.743
I could stand here all night
yelling out everything I know.

00:03:21.743 --> 00:03:22.953
I've already been dismissed from my post.

00:03:22.953 --> 00:03:25.831
Are you trying to threaten me, Uruz 7?

00:03:25.831 --> 00:03:28.667
I will report this officially
to the Tactical Division.

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:31.587
Do whatever you want.
But you will answer my question.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:35.966
My mission is to guard her, of course.

00:03:35.966 --> 00:03:37.259
I can't trust you.

00:03:37.259 --> 00:03:39.720
That's your choice.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.805
But the mission given to me

00:03:41.805 --> 00:03:45.642
was to prevent Kaname Chidori from falling
into the hands of another organization.

00:03:45.642 --> 00:03:47.811
Nothing more, nothing less.

00:03:47.811 --> 00:03:49.688
Then why don't you ever save her?

00:03:49.688 --> 00:03:52.232
She's been surrounded
by a gang of delinquents.

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.984
She's been abducted by a band of thugs.

00:03:53.984 --> 00:03:55.944
She's been in danger numerous times.

00:03:55.944 --> 00:03:59.239
Those were all the
acts of insignificant hoodlums.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:01.950
There was not enough
of a reason for me to act.

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:03.493
I see.

00:04:03.493 --> 00:04:06.580
Then how do you explain the A21 incident?

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:10.751
Even then, you didn't try to save her.

00:04:10.751 --> 00:04:13.170
How about that? Answer me!

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:15.881
My intent was to give the enemy
rope and see what they'd do,

00:04:15.881 --> 00:04:19.009
but things got out of my control.

00:04:19.009 --> 00:04:23.013
Even I broke into a cold sweat
during that hostage exchange,

00:04:23.013 --> 00:04:25.682
but my decision not to
interfere proved to be correct.

00:04:25.682 --> 00:04:31.688
I'm told those terrorists had no idea how
special or important she was, isn't that right?

00:04:31.688 --> 00:04:34.983
In other words, they were essentially
the same as a bunch of street hoodlums.

00:04:34.983 --> 00:04:35.943
That's nothing but sophistry.

00:04:35.943 --> 00:04:37.569
Call it whatever you want.

00:04:37.569 --> 00:04:40.948
Either way, the knowledge she
possesses was not brought out.

00:04:40.948 --> 00:04:43.700
That is the one thing that needs
to be protected in the first place.

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:46.370
As long as the enemy doesn't get close
to her in order to obtain her knowledge,

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:49.540
there is no particular need for me to act.

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:51.291
So your true nature shows.

00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:53.710
But if she died, everything would be lost.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:57.047
Of course, at the very minimum,
I will protect her life so that doesn't happen.

00:04:57.047 --> 00:04:58.382
I don't believe you.

00:04:58.382 --> 00:05:01.552
I don't really expect
you to believe me, anyway.

00:05:01.552 --> 00:05:05.180
So go ahead and worry yourself
to death about it for all I care.

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:08.559
This operation was originally supposed
to have been taken over by Intelligence

00:05:08.559 --> 00:05:10.727
after the Khanka Airport incident.

00:05:10.727 --> 00:05:15.524
But then Tactical interfered,
and made us let you stay.

00:05:15.524 --> 00:05:19.570
Tactical made the point that you
would be effective as a decoy,

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:22.823
but to me, you are nothing
more than an annoyance.

00:05:22.823 --> 00:05:25.033
You have no idea how many times
I've wanted to kill you off

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:26.827
and make it look like an accident.

00:05:26.827 --> 00:05:29.204
It's still not too late.
Go ahead and try.

00:05:29.204 --> 00:05:30.747
It was a joke.

00:05:30.747 --> 00:05:33.917
I don't think I could finish you
off without getting hurt myself.

00:05:33.917 --> 00:05:36.420
And actually, you have provided
me with some amusement.

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:37.546
What?

00:05:37.546 --> 00:05:43.051
Just aiming a rifle at you from a distance
is enough to make you extremely nervous.

00:05:43.051 --> 00:05:45.596
You have excellent instincts as a soldier,

00:05:45.596 --> 00:05:48.432
but those instincts have caused
you to fail numerous times, correct?

00:05:48.432 --> 00:05:52.477
That disturbance at the barber
shop today was quite entertaining.

00:05:52.477 --> 00:05:53.770
You bastard...

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:56.523
Don't get so angry.
It's in the past now.

00:05:56.523 --> 00:05:59.985
In any event, the fun is over as of today.

00:05:59.985 --> 00:06:03.071
You should return to base and
go back to your original mission.

00:06:03.071 --> 00:06:06.783
We are both pros. Don't you think
we should end this silly argument?

00:06:06.783 --> 00:06:09.578
I cannot. What about Chidori's safety?

00:06:09.578 --> 00:06:11.955
That is no longer any of your concern.

00:06:11.955 --> 00:06:14.666
You were sent official
orders to withdraw, correct?

00:06:15.918 --> 00:06:18.587
Surely you don't intend
to disobey orders, do you?

00:06:18.587 --> 00:06:19.963
Well...

00:06:19.963 --> 00:06:25.135
Do not forget that your life
here was provided by Mithril.

00:06:25.135 --> 00:06:27.804
You were never a high school
student or anything of the sort.

00:06:27.804 --> 00:06:30.140
You are just a mercenary,
a professional killer.

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:34.269
Your family registration and school
registration are fake, part of a disguise.

00:06:34.269 --> 00:06:37.105
What were you even thinking to begin with?

00:06:37.105 --> 00:06:42.110
You constantly have to leave her
to go on other missions, don't you?

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:48.659
How effective can you possibly be as a decoy
when you can't be with her full-time?

00:06:48.659 --> 00:06:53.413
Do you honestly think you
can protect her like that?

00:06:53.413 --> 00:06:55.499
Well? Tell me.

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:58.710
What's wrong?
Can't you answer?

00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:01.463
Or is it that you don't want to answer?

00:07:01.463 --> 00:07:04.091
Well, either way it doesn't matter.

00:07:04.091 --> 00:07:05.592
At any rate,

00:07:05.592 --> 00:07:08.178
regardless of whether or not
you have a gripe against me,

00:07:08.178 --> 00:07:12.808
in the end, you still have to
entrust her to me and leave Tokyo.

00:07:12.808 --> 00:07:15.769
The point is, nothing has changed, Uruz 7.

00:07:15.769 --> 00:07:18.105
Your absence simply means I've lost a decoy,

00:07:18.105 --> 00:07:23.861
and I will have to spend more time
than before guarding her myself.

00:07:23.861 --> 00:07:25.529
That's all.

00:07:25.529 --> 00:07:28.031
Really, you criticize me,

00:07:28.031 --> 00:07:32.494
but do you seriously believe someone
like you could possibly protect her?

00:07:33.829 --> 00:07:35.163
In these past six months,

00:07:35.163 --> 00:07:38.333
you haven't been able to adapt
to Japanese society at all.

00:07:38.333 --> 00:07:42.212
Your presence is putting
her in danger unnecessarily.

00:07:42.212 --> 00:07:43.839
Sorry to say this,

00:07:43.839 --> 00:07:46.884
but as a bodyguard,
you are lower than third rate.

00:07:46.884 --> 00:07:49.803
In the end, to her, you're
nothing but a harmful influence.

00:07:49.803 --> 00:07:53.015
Not only that, you'd probably
endanger the people around her too.

00:07:53.015 --> 00:07:55.225
You have no right to talk to me like that!

00:07:55.225 --> 00:07:58.979
Pissed off because I hit
the nail right on the head?

00:07:58.979 --> 00:08:02.566
Either way, this little game
of house is over, Uruz 7.

00:08:02.566 --> 00:08:04.401
Obey your orders and return to base.

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:18.457
Caw! It's morning!

00:08:18.457 --> 00:08:19.750
Caw! Wake up!

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:21.251
Caw! Kana-<i>chan</i>, you'll be...

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:06.296
Good morning, Kyoko!

00:09:06.296 --> 00:09:07.714
Oh, good morning!

00:09:07.714 --> 00:09:09.716
You seem happy today, Kana-<i>chan</i>!

00:09:09.716 --> 00:09:10.509
Really?

00:09:10.509 --> 00:09:13.303
Yeah. Did something good happen?

00:09:13.303 --> 00:09:14.930
No, not really.

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:16.515
Was there something?

00:09:16.515 --> 00:09:18.559
I wonder if it's even
worth mentioning, though?

00:09:20.561 --> 00:09:21.979
You're acting weird.

00:09:21.979 --> 00:09:25.732
At any rate, Sagara was being his
usual self yesterday, wasn't he?

00:09:25.732 --> 00:09:28.777
Really. He never makes
any progress, does he?

00:09:28.777 --> 00:09:30.988
It makes me want to put a
remote-controlled electric shock device

00:09:30.988 --> 00:09:32.906
in his brain or something.

00:09:32.906 --> 00:09:36.326
And every time he messes up:
Bzzt! Bzzt! It'll zap him!

00:09:36.326 --> 00:09:38.453
That might actually have some effect.

00:09:38.453 --> 00:09:39.913
So, what do you think, Kyoko?

00:09:39.913 --> 00:09:42.583
He's not a dog, you know.

00:09:42.583 --> 00:09:44.751
Oh, speaking of which,
what happened after that?

00:09:44.751 --> 00:09:47.838
Huh? We... We went home. Why?

00:09:47.838 --> 00:09:50.299
Then, I wonder what he's
going to do about a haircut.

00:09:50.299 --> 00:09:53.177
You're right.
He'll probably just cut it himself.

00:09:53.177 --> 00:09:55.345
Then it'll get all bushy again.

00:09:56.972 --> 00:09:59.683
<i>I have to make sure our</i>
<i>stories match up later.</i>

00:10:00.976 --> 00:10:04.855
But someone seems really
cheerful today for some reason.

00:10:04.855 --> 00:10:05.647
Who?

00:10:05.647 --> 00:10:06.607
You, Kana-<i>chan</i>!

00:10:06.607 --> 00:10:09.860
What? That's just your imagination.

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:12.029
Hmm, something seems suspicious here!

00:10:12.029 --> 00:10:14.656
I'm telling you,
nothing happened, honestly.

00:10:14.656 --> 00:10:17.659
Anyway, did you see
Kumodoushin the other day?

00:10:17.659 --> 00:10:19.369
Well, yeah, but...

00:10:19.369 --> 00:10:20.370
How was it?

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:22.623
Umm, to be honest,
I didn't really like it.

00:10:22.623 --> 00:10:23.957
Huh? Why not?

00:10:23.957 --> 00:10:25.000
No real reason.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:29.338
--The action scene with the octopus samurai was good, though.
--Yeah, that part!

00:10:29.338 --> 00:10:33.717
Those weird tentacles came out of
his back! That was the best part!

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:38.889
Right. And then...

00:10:38.889 --> 00:10:41.391
--Anyway, it's<i> really </i>amazing!
--What's wrong?

00:10:41.391 --> 00:10:42.392
It's nothing.

00:10:42.392 --> 00:10:45.729
I didn't know about it either,
but it looks like it has a continuation.

00:10:45.729 --> 00:10:46.813
Good morning Kazama.

00:10:46.813 --> 00:10:48.148
Good morning, Miss Chidori.

00:10:48.148 --> 00:10:48.982
Where's Sousuke?

00:10:48.982 --> 00:10:52.236
Dunno. I haven't seen him yet today.

00:10:52.236 --> 00:10:54.988
Then I guess he hasn't come yet.
That's good.

00:10:56.073 --> 00:10:56.907
What happened?

00:10:56.907 --> 00:10:59.409
Oh, nothing.

00:10:59.409 --> 00:11:00.953
Did something happen?

00:11:00.953 --> 00:11:02.329
Beats me.

00:11:04.748 --> 00:11:05.749
Good morning!

00:11:05.749 --> 00:11:07.376
Oh, good morning.

00:11:11.338 --> 00:11:14.716
That was close!
I just made it!

00:11:22.933 --> 00:11:24.393
I wonder what he's doing?

00:11:26.061 --> 00:11:28.063
Rise!

00:11:28.063 --> 00:11:28.981
Bow!

00:11:28.981 --> 00:11:31.191
--Good morning, sir.
--Good morning.

00:11:31.191 --> 00:11:32.276
Take your seat!

00:11:33.944 --> 00:11:35.445
All right, I'm going to take attendance.

00:11:35.445 --> 00:11:37.114
--Igarashi.
--Here!

00:11:37.114 --> 00:11:38.740
--Ishihara.
--Here!

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:40.325
--Isomura.
--Here!

00:11:40.325 --> 00:11:41.994
--Uozumi.
--Here.

00:11:41.994 --> 00:11:43.412
--Uchida.
--Here!

00:11:43.412 --> 00:11:45.122
--Oumi.
--Here!

00:11:45.122 --> 00:11:46.999
--Ogata.
--Here.

00:13:08.830 --> 00:13:09.831
"Letter of Resignation from School To
the Principal of Jindai High School:

00:13:09.831 --> 00:13:11.041
Due to personal matters, I will be resigning
from school. Class 2-4 Sousuke Sagara"

00:13:16.630 --> 00:13:17.881
"Chidori, Kaname"

00:13:26.306 --> 00:13:27.850
"Chidori, Kaname"

00:13:32.312 --> 00:13:33.355
"Kana"

00:13:37.401 --> 00:13:39.903
Hmm, he's not answering?

00:13:39.903 --> 00:13:43.198
No. He seems to have
it turned on, though.

00:13:43.198 --> 00:13:44.533
I wonder what's wrong?

00:13:44.533 --> 00:13:48.078
Who knows. What in the world
is that idiot doing?

00:13:52.749 --> 00:13:54.543
"Missed calls:
Chidori, Kaname"

00:13:58.213 --> 00:13:59.965
Orders...

00:14:02.926 --> 00:14:03.844
Dammit.

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:28.452
Dammit.

00:14:30.037 --> 00:14:32.623
Ka-na-<i>chan</i>!

00:14:32.623 --> 00:14:35.125
It's all over for me!

00:14:35.125 --> 00:14:36.585
You did that badly?

00:14:36.585 --> 00:14:40.881
Yeah. I did horrible on the Math II
test we were handed back today.

00:14:40.881 --> 00:14:44.092
There, there. It's not like
your whole life depends on it.

00:14:44.092 --> 00:14:45.844
How did you do, Kana-<i>chan</i>?

00:14:45.844 --> 00:14:50.098
Me? I did... so-so, I guess.

00:14:50.098 --> 00:14:52.601
You traitor.

00:14:52.601 --> 00:14:53.644
Now that I think about it,

00:14:53.644 --> 00:14:57.731
you got the top scores in the last science
and math final exams too, didn't you?

00:14:57.731 --> 00:14:59.149
Yeah.

00:14:59.149 --> 00:15:01.902
Well, it was just a fluke, just a fluke.

00:15:01.902 --> 00:15:04.655
I wonder if it's because of
my abilities as a Whispered?

00:15:04.655 --> 00:15:06.823
What? Do you know
some sort of trick to it?

00:15:06.823 --> 00:15:09.076
Huh? N-Not really.

00:15:09.076 --> 00:15:14.456
Really? Hey, how do you study?
Or could you be cheating?

00:15:14.456 --> 00:15:19.253
Well anyway, whatever it is,
I don't care, just tell me!

00:15:19.253 --> 00:15:20.295
It's a secret.

00:15:20.295 --> 00:15:22.172
You are not authorized to know that.

00:15:22.172 --> 00:15:23.924
Just kidding!

00:15:25.634 --> 00:15:29.346
Hey, Sagara didn't come after all.

00:15:29.346 --> 00:15:30.681
Yeah, you're right.

00:15:30.681 --> 00:15:34.101
I wonder if that idiot is<i> trying </i>to fail.

00:15:34.101 --> 00:15:36.353
He's already in big trouble.

00:15:37.563 --> 00:15:41.024
Hey, why don't you try
calling him one more time?

00:15:41.024 --> 00:15:42.484
He might answer this time.

00:15:42.484 --> 00:15:44.528
Hmm...

00:15:49.700 --> 00:15:53.704
Well, he's been out of
touch a lot of times before.

00:15:53.704 --> 00:15:56.081
It's not something to get
worried about every single time!

00:15:56.081 --> 00:15:57.875
Really?

00:15:57.875 --> 00:16:00.669
If you say so, I guess that's okay.

00:16:00.669 --> 00:16:02.713
Uh-huh. That's right.

00:16:02.713 --> 00:16:05.465
More importantly, the tests are over,

00:16:05.465 --> 00:16:07.467
so why don't we go have
some fun while we can?

00:16:07.467 --> 00:16:09.720
We'll invite everyone,
and sing karaoke and stuff!

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:11.597
Yeah, that sounds good.

00:16:11.597 --> 00:16:15.017
We'll do what we haven't done in a while:
a ten-hour karaoke marathon!

00:16:15.017 --> 00:16:17.060
What? That again?

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:19.521
What? It was fun, wasn't it?

00:16:19.521 --> 00:16:22.024
Umm, well, that's true, but...

00:16:22.024 --> 00:16:24.026
We were all exhausted the next day.

00:16:24.026 --> 00:16:25.903
Who cares?

00:16:25.903 --> 00:16:28.822
Singing and singing until
you can't even move anymore!

00:16:28.822 --> 00:16:31.950
Such a sense of accomplishment!
Such a feeling of exhaustion!

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:33.410
What are you talking about?

00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:34.494
All right, it's decided!

00:16:34.494 --> 00:16:36.413
We're all going to do a
ten hour karaoke marathon!

00:16:36.413 --> 00:16:38.332
And you absolutely
must participate, Kyoko!

00:16:40.292 --> 00:16:43.086
Okay, so who should we invite?

00:16:43.086 --> 00:16:48.425
Shiori and Maya and
Miss Ren and Mizuki and...

00:16:51.094 --> 00:16:51.762
Huh?

00:16:59.728 --> 00:17:02.314
What... was that?

00:17:02.314 --> 00:17:04.441
Kana-<i>chan</i>?

00:17:11.281 --> 00:17:13.784
Hey, Kana-<i>chan</i>?

00:17:17.746 --> 00:17:19.957
Hey, what's wrong?

00:17:19.957 --> 00:17:22.042
Hey! Hey, come on!

00:17:29.174 --> 00:17:30.342
Kana-<i>chan</i>...

00:17:31.426 --> 00:17:35.305
<i>It's okay, it's okay. It's okay, it's okay.</i>

00:17:35.305 --> 00:17:39.434
The number you have
dialed cannot be reached,

00:17:39.434 --> 00:17:42.938
due to being out of the service area,
or the power being off.

00:17:42.938 --> 00:17:45.107
The number you have
dialed cannot be reached...

00:17:49.528 --> 00:17:50.696
Are you okay?

00:17:50.696 --> 00:17:53.073
I'm sorry, Kyoko. I'm going home.

00:17:53.073 --> 00:17:54.408
You're kidding!

00:17:55.576 --> 00:17:58.245
I can't just let you go when
you're acting like this!

00:17:58.245 --> 00:17:59.371
--It's okay.
--But!

00:17:59.371 --> 00:18:01.081
I said it's okay!

00:18:02.207 --> 00:18:03.834
Sorry.

00:18:03.834 --> 00:18:05.169
See you tomorrow.

00:18:05.169 --> 00:18:06.670
Yeah...

00:18:41.872 --> 00:18:43.707
Okay, it's begun!

00:18:43.707 --> 00:18:44.374
Finally!

00:18:44.374 --> 00:18:46.543
Let's start right off by
introducing the guest of the week!

00:18:46.543 --> 00:18:48.879
Everyone meet the An Doughnuts!

00:18:52.174 --> 00:18:53.800
Hi, we're the An Doughnuts.

00:18:53.800 --> 00:18:55.719
The totally creepy but cute An Doughnuts.

00:18:55.719 --> 00:18:57.763
Hold it, whaddya mean by creepy-cute?

00:18:57.763 --> 00:19:00.182
But right now,
we're kinda creepy-cute, you know?

00:19:00.182 --> 00:19:03.435
What did you say? Take this!

00:19:09.399 --> 00:19:11.443
Ta-dah!

00:19:18.283 --> 00:19:19.868
Take that! Take that!

00:19:28.919 --> 00:19:32.297
It's okay. It's nothing.
It's okay. It's nothing.

00:19:32.297 --> 00:19:33.674
It's okay. It's noth...

00:20:27.769 --> 00:20:30.272
Yes? This is Chidori.

00:20:30.981 --> 00:20:32.441
Hello?

00:20:33.525 --> 00:20:37.529
Hey, who are you?

00:20:37.613 --> 00:20:38.363
<i>"Unknown Caller"</i>

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:45.287
Sousuke!

00:20:49.791 --> 00:20:51.835
--The number you have dialed...
--Damn it!

00:20:54.254 --> 00:20:56.340
How...

00:20:56.340 --> 00:20:58.300
How can I contact him?

00:20:58.300 --> 00:20:59.927
Oh yeah! The communicator!

00:21:10.521 --> 00:21:13.357
<i>Mithril uses a satellite</i>
<i>circuit that incorporates</i>

00:21:13.357 --> 00:21:16.485
<i>a spectrum diffusion modulation process</i>

00:21:16.485 --> 00:21:17.986
<i>and a unique quantum code.</i>

00:21:17.986 --> 00:21:20.364
<i>Thanks to the time I spent</i>
<i>on the Tuatha de Danaan,</i>

00:21:20.364 --> 00:21:23.575
<i>I know the details of the method</i>
<i>and the general frequency band.</i>

00:21:23.575 --> 00:21:25.702
<i>I'm sure I can do this!</i>

00:21:25.702 --> 00:21:27.371
Sousuke, are you there?

00:21:32.543 --> 00:21:34.044
"Classics Kaname Chidori"

00:21:34.044 --> 00:21:36.380
My notebook...

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:38.715
What was this doing lying there?

00:21:46.056 --> 00:21:47.349
Huh?

00:22:06.159 --> 00:22:07.995
No way...

00:22:27.764 --> 00:22:29.516
<i>I'm sure you're still looking</i>

00:22:29.516 --> 00:22:33.312
<i>Straight ahead to tomorrow</i>

00:22:33.312 --> 00:22:39.193
<i>Just like you always have</i>

00:22:39.193 --> 00:22:44.907
<i>Just like the sunflowers</i>

00:22:44.907 --> 00:22:51.663
<i>That bloomed on that windy hill</i>

00:22:53.582 --> 00:22:59.505
<i>No matter how far apart we are</i>

00:22:59.505 --> 00:23:05.511
<i>I pray that my singing will reach you</i>

00:23:05.511 --> 00:23:11.558
<i>On nights when the tears never seem to stop</i>

00:23:11.558 --> 00:23:14.895
<i>I want to be the moon</i>

00:23:14.895 --> 00:23:17.898
<i>That shines through your window</i>

00:23:17.898 --> 00:23:25.948
<i>Because I believe we will meet again</i>

00:23:28.283 --> 00:23:31.870
<i>No matter what</i>

00:23:45.259 --> 00:23:46.885
"Next Episode"

00:23:46.885 --> 00:23:49.847
<i>Violent frustration. Disputes and tears.</i>

00:23:49.847 --> 00:23:53.600
<i>Pure hatred rises within me for the</i>
<i>machine that tore me apart from her.</i>

00:23:53.600 --> 00:23:57.437
<i>Little do I know that it will</i>
<i>become a curse on myself.</i>

00:23:57.437 --> 00:23:59.815
<i>Next time: "Jungle Groove"</i>

00:23:59.815 --> 00:24:04.715
<i>Black and white flashes</i>
<i>pierce through the jungle.</i>
